{
  "_comment": [
    "Fuigo ships FluxRouter lanes, not vendor model ids. One sk-flux- key reaches",
    "Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek, Moonshot and the rest.",
    "",
    "CONTEXT WINDOW POLICY — read before editing a context_window.",
    "",
    "The hazard is specific to ROUTED lanes, not to FluxRouter's numbers.",
    "A pinned model's advertised window is accurate: flux-pinned-claude-opus-5",
    "reports 1000000, and Claude Opus 5 genuinely is a 1M-token model. Verified",
    "2026-09-01 against Anthropic's model docs. (An earlier revision of this file",
    "capped it at 200000 on the strength of an out-of-date figure and silently",
    "threw away 800k of context.)",
    "",
    "An AUTO lane is different. `flux-auto` advertises 1000000 because that is",
    "the ceiling of its routing pool, not a promise about any one request. A live",
    "flux-auto call routed to qwen-plus, whose real window is 129024. Size against",
    "the advertised 1000000 and auto-compaction never fires -- the wedge that grew",
    "a Wayland Core session to 17M cumulative input tokens (their #255).",
    "",
    "So: floor the routed lanes, trust the pins. Per-request truth is in the",
    "x-flux-model-window header, which does track the model actually served.",
    "Note also that 29 of 79 catalogue entries omit max_input_tokens entirely;",
    "for those there is nothing to trust and 128000 is the safe assumption."
  ],
  "default": "flux-auto",
  "web_search": "flux-fast",
  "image_description": "flux-fast",
  "session_summary": "flux-fast",
  "models": [
    {
